### 3.3 В `decode_ogg()` сначала пытаться декодировать stash (если есть)
Файл: `flac_decoder.cpp`, в начале `while(true)` в `decode_ogg` (после `remaining = input_len - bytes_consumed;` и до вызова `get_next_data`) вставить:

```cpp
// If we have stashed leftover bytes from a previous Ogg packet, decode them first.
// Stash bytes were already consumed from input in a previous call, so this consumes 0 new input bytes.
if (!this->ogg_stash_.empty()) {
    size_t native_consumed = 0;
    size_t native_samples = 0;
    auto result = this->decode_native(this->ogg_stash_.data(), this->ogg_stash_.size(),
                                      output, native_consumed, native_samples, output_32bit);
    samples_decoded = native_samples;
    this->last_ogg_body_len_ = this->ogg_stash_.size();
    this->last_ogg_native_consumed_ = native_consumed;

    if (native_consumed > 0) {
        // erase consumed prefix
        this->ogg_stash_.erase(this->ogg_stash_.begin(),
                               this->ogg_stash_.begin() + (ptrdiff_t)native_consumed);
    }

    if (result == FLAC_DECODER_NEED_MORE_DATA) {
        // Need more bytes: fall through to pull more data from ogg demuxer and continue
    } else {
        return result;  // SUCCESS / HEADER_READY / error
    }
}
```

### 3.4 В Step 3: при SUCCESS/HEADER_READY и `native_consumed < body_len` — stash remainder, НЕ фаталить
Файл: `flac_decoder.cpp`, в `decode_ogg` в Step 3 (где сейчас upstream-логика “если native_consumed != body_len -> OGG_DEMUX”), заменить только этот участок на:

```cpp
this->last_ogg_body_len_ = body_len;
this->last_ogg_native_consumed_ = native_consumed;

// If decode_native produced a result but didn't consume all offered bytes,
// stash the remainder and treat the packet bytes as consumed.
if ((result == FLAC_DECODER_SUCCESS || result == FLAC_DECODER_HEADER_READY) && native_consumed < body_len) {
    const size_t rem = body_len - native_consumed;
    // safety cap to avoid runaway memory usage
    if (rem > 0 && rem <= 65535) {
        this->ogg_stash_.insert(this->ogg_stash_.end(), body + native_consumed, body + body_len);
        native_consumed = body_len;
    } else {
        return this->set_fatal_error(FLAC_DECODER_ERROR_OGG_DEMUX);
    }
}

// Keep the original invariant check for unexpected cases
if (native_consumed != body_len) {
    return this->set_fatal_error(FLAC_DECODER_ERROR_OGG_DEMUX);
}

if (result == FLAC_DECODER_NEED_MORE_DATA) {
    continue;
}
if (result == FLAC_DECODER_HEADER_READY) {
    return FLAC_DECODER_HEADER_READY;
}
if (result == FLAC_DECODER_SUCCESS) {
    return FLAC_DECODER_SUCCESS;
}
if (result == FLAC_DECODER_END_OF_STREAM) {
    return FLAC_DECODER_END_OF_STREAM;
}
return result;
```

